{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A converter from standard notation pitches (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/Pitch","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") to MIDI note numbers ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/NoteNumber"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"using a keyboard layout, tuning system, and pitch standard.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"externalID":"s:10IvorTuning32StandardToKeyboardPitchConverterV","title":"StandardToKeyboardPitchConverter","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StandardToKeyboardPitchConverter","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StandardToKeyboardPitchConverter"}]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/StandardToKeyboardPitchConverter\/init()","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/StandardToKeyboardPitchConverter\/init(keyboardLayout:tuningSystem:pitchStandard:keyMatching:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/StandardToKeyboardPitchConverter\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/StandardToKeyboardPitchConverter\/PitchConverter-Implementations"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StandardToKeyboardPitchConverter","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/UsingIvorTuning"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversion is acoustic: the converter realizes each pitch as a frequency using the tuning system"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and pitch standard, then picks the key of the layout that sounds nearest. The keys are tuned by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same tuning system and pitch standard, so the pitch standard tunes the keyboard rather than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transposing it: with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/PitchStandard\/a415","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", A4 still converts to 69, and key 69 sounds 415 Hz.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With the default configuration — "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/KeyboardLayout\/piano"},{"type":"text","text":", 12-tone equal temperament, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/PitchStandard\/a440"},{"type":"text","text":" — this matches the usual piano key assignments, so B♯3 and C4 both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"convert to 60, and C♭4 to 59. With other tuning systems, a pitch may convert to a key other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than the one its spelling suggests: in quarter-comma meantone, B𝄪3 sounds about 45 cents above","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"C4 — nearer the C key than the C♯ key — so it converts to 60, not 61.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a pitch lies equally near two keys of a pitch-class layout, it converts to the key whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spelling shares its letter; otherwise, to the lower key."}]}]}],"relationshipsSection